# Denali tour mutation safety

## Problem

Operator flat-edit `PATCH /tours/:id` historically allowed **any** canonical field change even when registrations existed. Member intake snapshots freeze on approve (`DN-READ-05`), but live tour fields (price, schedule, capacity, transport) could diverge without notify, reprice workflow, or capacity guardrails.

DP-3 centralizes mutation policy so UI disabled controls are **not** the security boundary.

## Evaluator shape

```text
current tour canonical.data
+ proposed patch (merged preview)
+ operational facts (bookings)
+ optional operatorMutationOverride (owner)
→ mutation decision
```

| Decision | Meaning |
| -------- | ------- |
| `ALLOW` | Persist patch |
| `DENY` | Reject with stable HTTP code + reason |
| `REQUIRE_OVERRIDE` | Reject unless `operatorMutationOverride: true` **and** workspace owner |
| `ALLOW_WITH_SIDE_EFFECT` | Persist + enqueue outbox side effects (never silent finance mutation) |

Operational facts (host port):

| Fact | Source |
| ---- | ------ |
| `activeRegistrationCount` | `pending` + `approved` + `waitlisted` on tour |
| `approvedRegistrationCount` | `status=approved` |
| `paidRegistrationCount` | `paymentStatus ∈ {paid, partial}` |
| `occupiedApprovedPartySize` | sum `partySize` where `approved` |
| `hasTransportAllocations` | canonical `transport.allocations` non-empty (DP-5 bridge until assignment SoT lands) |

When `activeRegistrationCount === 0`, policy returns `ALLOW` for all fields (no-registration tours remain freely editable).

## Field class matrix (DEN-PROD-10 approved)

Logical canonical path → class. Data paths follow Denali field registry (`zodPath`).

| Canonical path | Class | Notes |
| -------------- | ----- | ----- |
| `title`, `program.shortDescription`, `photos`, `program.itinerary`, `participants.gearItems` | `SAFE_MUTABLE` | Content edits after registrations |
| `destinationId`, `category`, `eventVariant`, `duration` | `FROZEN_AFTER_REGISTRATION` | Any active registration |
| `pricing.basePricePerPerson`, `pricing.prepaymentPercent`, `pricing.paymentMode`, `pricing.requiresPayment` | `FROZEN_AFTER_APPROVAL` → repricing workflow when unpaid approved exist; `FROZEN_AFTER_PAYMENT` when paid/partial exist |
| `startDateTime`, `endDateTime`, `tripDetails.logistics.gatheringPoints` | `MUTABLE_WITH_NOTIFICATION` | Emits `tour.mutation.notification_required` |
| `capacityMax` decrease | `REQUIRES_OPERATOR_OVERRIDE` when regs exist; **DENY** if new max &lt; occupied approved party size |
| `capacityMax` increase | `ALLOW` | |
| `transport.*` | `REQUIRES_OPERATOR_OVERRIDE` when `hasTransportAllocations`; else `SAFE_MUTABLE` for mode copy-only before allocations |
| `publishStatus` | existing publish gate | Not reclassified here |

## HTTP errors

| Code | Status | When |
| ---- | ------ | ---- |
| `DENALI_TOUR_MUTATION_BLOCKED` | 409 | `DENY` |
| `DENALI_TOUR_MUTATION_OVERRIDE_REQUIRED` | 409 | `REQUIRE_OVERRIDE` without owner override |

Response body includes `reasonCode`, `fields[]`, optional `sideEffects[]` for operator UI.

## Side effects (post-persist outbox)

| Event | When |
| ----- | ---- |
| `tour.mutation.notification_required` | Schedule / logistics `MUTABLE_WITH_NOTIFICATION` |
| `tour.mutation.repricing_required` | Price change with approved-unpaid registrations (no ledger mutation) |
| `tour.mutation.transport_review_required` | Transport change when allocations locked |

Finance obligation / refund flows are **not** mutated silently — DP-1 freeze + DP-6 own money paths.

**Post-persist enqueue (Prisma):** `emitTourMutationSideEffects` writes via `persistStandaloneOutboxRowIfPrismaDriver`, which **must** call `withTenantRls(tenantId, …)` before `outbox_events` insert. Outbox RLS `WITH CHECK` compares `tenant_id` to `current_setting('app.current_tenant_id')::uuid`; a bare Prisma client without session bind yields invalid UUID cast / silent insert failure on schedule mutations.

## Write path

Enforced in `CanonicalTourService.updateTourInActiveContext` **after** merge + pre-TX validation, **before** persist. Denali rules live in `@app-tour/workspace-denali` `tour-mutation-policy`; API supplies facts + override authorization + outbox enqueue.

## Verification

- Domain: `packages/workspaces/denali/test/tour-mutation-policy.spec.ts`
- API: `apps/api/test/dp3/tour-mutation-enforcement.spec.ts`
- Gate: `scripts/test-dp3-tour-mutation.sh`
